# Without this file setuptools falls back to its default sdist selection, which
# picks up `tests/test_*.py` by pattern and SILENTLY OMITS `tests/conftest.py`.
# That produced an sdist whose tests directory looked complete and could not run:
# every fixture the suite depends on (primary_fasta, control_fasta, small_fasta,
# motif_db, requires_meme, PLANTED_MOTIF) is defined in conftest.py, so a source
# install collected six test modules and errored on all of them.
#
# The suite ships deliberately. This package's claim is that the wrappers are
# verified against the REAL MEME binaries rather than a mock, and a user
# installing from source should be able to re-run that check against their own
# MEME install. Shipping half a suite serves neither goal.
#
# tests/ is excluded from the WHEEL by [tool.setuptools.packages.find] — only
# the sdist carries it, which is the conventional split.
recursive-include tests *.py
